<title>JAPAN: Japan March beef imports down 10.8 pct yr/yr - MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan March beef imports down 10.8 pct yr/yr - MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's beef imports in March totalled 35,581 tonnes, down 10.8 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>The details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Mar 97	 Feb 97     Mar 96</p>
<p> Total	    35,581	 39,313     39,898</p>
<p> Refrigerated   25,032	 26,201     27,604</p>
<p> Frozen	   10,549	 13,112     12,294</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>  Australia     14,471	 15,905     15,957</p>
<p>  U.S.	     9,634	  9,405	6,900</p>
<p>Major suppliers of frozen beef (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Mar 97	 Feb 97	Mar 96</p>
<p> U.S.		4,508	   6,665     6,550</p>
<p> Australia	 5,059	   4,764     4,806</p>
<p>Cumulative imports of refrigerated beef in the first three months of 1997 were 72,195 tonnes against 78,676 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>Frozen beef imports in the January-March period of this year were 43,240 tonnes against 53,223 tonnes in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
